    "report_md": "### Incident Report: LSASS Process Memory Access (T1003.001)\n\nAn alert was triggered on host `workstation5` indicating LSASS process memory access by `rundll32.exe`. Investigation revealed that PowerShell launched `rundll32.exe` with the command line loading `comsvcs.dll` to create a full memory dump of the LSASS process (`lsass-comsvcs.dmp`) under the user `wardog`'s temporary directory.\n\nThis technique is commonly used by adversaries to harvest credentials from LSASS memory.\n\n**Verdict:** True Positive\n**Technique:** T1003.001 (OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory)"
